/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A sensor converts a physical quantity into an electrical signal.
   - Specifications decide whether a sensor suits a job.
   - Behind these classes sit a few physical effects.
   - Signal conditioning is everything between the sensing element and the ADC.
   - Vout = Vs × Rs / (Rs + Rf)
   - Vout is the junction voltage in volts; Vs is the supply voltage in volts; Rs is the sensing resistance in ohms, connected from Vout to ground; Rf is the fixed resistor in ohms, connected from +Vs to Vout.
*/
