/* book exam traps: The ADC count is not the physical value. 682 is a voltage code, not 25 °C; convert and linearise with the sensor curve before quoting a temperature. | NTC resistance falls with temperature, so the divider output falls with temperature. Many answers show the voltage rising and lose all the marks. | Sensitivity must carry units (mV/°C, mV/kPa). | Resolution is not accuracy. A 10-bit ADC resolves 4.89 mV, but the sensor may still be accurate only to ±2 °C; reference tolerance and self-heating add further error. | Self-heating: the excitation current warms the thermistor, so it reads hotter than the fluid. Keep the current small (a pull-up of a few kΩ). */
